      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-11-22_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <p>In Parliament—Session 1902,</p>
        <p>LANCISHIRE COUNTY (LUNATIC ASYLUMS).</p>
        <p>Alteration of Mode of Contribution to the Asylums Fund by Lancashire County Council and County Boroughs ; Alteration and Amendment of Lanca- shire County (Lunatic Asylums and other powers) Act 1891 and Repeal of Portions of that Act ; Re- turns by Clerks to Boards of Guardians ; Repeal and Amendment of Acts ; Costs of Act. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that Application will be made to Parliament in the ensuing Session by the Mayor, Aldermen, and Citizens of the City of Man- chester, and the Mayor, Aldermen and Burgesses of the County Boroughs of Barrow-in-Furness, Blackburn, Bcotle, Burnley, Bury, Oldharn, Preston, Salford, St Helens, Stockport and Warrington (hereinafter referred to as " the promoters ") for leave to bring in a Bill for the following purposes or some of them (that is to say)— lo Alter the present Basis of Contribution by the Lancashire County Council and the County Boroughs as defined and referred to in the Lancashire County I (Lunatic Asylums and other powers) Act 1891 (herein- after referred to as the Alt of 1891) to the maintenance of the Lancashire County Lunatic Asylums and to pro- vide for the future contributions by the County Coun- cil and the said County Boroughs to the Lancashire Asylums Fund. To Repeal so much of the Act of 1891 as provides for the apportionment of the total amount required for the purposes of the Lancashire Asylums Board and the main- tenance of the Lancashire County Lunatic Asylums (hereinafter referred to as "the Asylums Board ' and "the Asylums" respectively) between the County and the said County Boroughs according to the respective rateab I values of the County and the said County Boroughs and particularly to repeal alter or amend sec- tions 24, 25 and 34 of the Act of 1891. To amend subsection (1) of section 26 of the Act of 1891 by substituting therein the words "the first day of April in every year ' in place of the words " the first day of March in every year." To give effect to certain resolutions passed at meet- ings of representatives of the Lancashire County Boroughs held] at the Town Ban, l,ancbester, en the 15th day of March and the 16th day of April, 1901. To provide for the future contributions to the Asy- lums Board and to the maintenance of the Asylums by the Lancashire County Council and the said County Boroughs in each year in proportion to number and the period of residence of lunatics sent by the County Council and the said County Boroughs respectively to be Asylums in each year. To providb for the making out by the Clerks of the Boards of Guardians in which the said County Boroughs respectively are situate of returns of the number of lunatics sent to the Asylums from the districts of the County Council and the County Boroughs respectively in each year and to prescribe a form for such returns and to provide for the furnishing of copies of such returns to the County Council of Lancashire and the said County Boroughs respectively. To provide for the inclusion in such lists of all lunatics sent to the Asylums and boarded out or sent to other Asylums or places other than Asylums by the Board. To provide for the making of annual estimates by the Asylums Board of the total amount required to be raised by contributions to the Asylums Fowl and for the annual apportionment of such total amalmt between the County Council and the County Boroughs and to fix the date for the commencement of such contributions. To provide that the provisions of the Local Loans Act, 1375, shall be available to the Asylums Board for the purpose of raising money under the Act of 1891. and to prescribe the period for repayment of loans se raised. To:authorise the said County Boroughs or any of them to invest any moneys in their hands standing to the credit of any sinking fund or other account in the mortgage or debenture securities of the Asylums Board. To amend the provisions of sections 23 and 37 sub- section (4) of the Act of 1891 and to apply those provi- sions to the intended Act. To amend so far as may be necessary for the purposes aforesaid all or some of the provisions of the Local Government Act 1388, the Lunacy Acts 1890 and 1891, and the Act of 1891, and to save all rights and liabilities under any orders made by the :lomrni=sioners appointed under the Local Government Act, 1888. To provide for payment and apportionment of the costs charges and expenses preliminary to and of and incidental to the preparing for and passing of the Bill among the promoters or 'among the promoters and Such others of the said County Boroughs as may be defined by the Bill. Printed copies cf the Bill will be deposited in the Private Bill Office of the HOMO of Commons on or before the 21st day of December next. Dated this day 15th day of November, 1901. ROBERT E. FOX, Town Clerk, Blackburn, Solicitor for the Bill ; TAHOURDINS &amp; HITCHCOCK, 20 Victoria-street, Westminster, Parliamentary Agents.</p>
