      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-11-22_WidnesExaminer_art0030" n="art0030">
        <head>TESTIMONY</head>
        <p>TESTIMONY</p>
        <p>An instance of the danger attending the indiscriminate use of cough lozenges has just been investigated in Liverpool. Most Liverpool people are familiar with a kind of lozenge, not free from dangerous ingredients, which can be purchased at many shops, even those of confectioners, in Liverpool. Made in the form of a palatable sweetmeat, this particular lozenge is not only in demand by adults, who understand to a certain extent its composition, but by younger people and children, who acquire thereby a most regretable taste for narcotics.</p>
        <p>A case in point has just occurred in the Stanley-road district. " I got such a liking at one time for ehlorodyne lozenges that I used to buy them and eat them like ordinary sweets. In fact, I was seldom without them." Such was the frank admission of a young lady whom a represen- tative questioned. _ _ _</p>
        <p>" Are you still in the habit of eating them P" asked the reporter. "No; was the prompt reply, "I haven t had any for along time now.' "I will tell you how it Was," interrupted the girl's mother (Mrs. Wood, 11, Orwell-road, Stanley-road t North.) "A boy died at Eastham through eating this kind of lozenge, and that frightened my daughter, and she has never had one of the lozenges since. I always think that her illness began through eating so many of them, and also with being very much indoors whilst'working as a dressmaker."</p>
        <p>" Oh! Was she seriously ill ? " "Yes, she was. Symptoms of s strange, distressing character commiloced to show themselves. She gradually became very wearied</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-11-22_WidnesExaminer_art0031" n="art0031">
        <head>Of no other</head>
        <p>Of no other</p>
        <p>that</p>
        <p>they MAKE BLOOD.</p>
        <p>Medical Science demands Proof. The value of a medicine is to be estimated by what it is Proved to 'Cure: not by what it is said to cure. Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People are used all over the United Kingdom because they are kno*n to cure. Not a word has ever been published concerning them that has not been accompanied by</p>
        <p>Proof.</p>
