      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-11-22_WidnesExaminer_art0111" n="art0111">
        <head>GOOD THINGS OF LIFE.</head>
        <p>THE GOOD THINGS OF LIFE.</p>
        <p>Many peop'e after enjoying the good things of life are subjeet to much after suffering from the inability of the stomach to perform its duties. A timely use of Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters would strengthen the digestive organs and serve to remedy the evil. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is the Best Remedy of the age for Indi- nestion, Weakness, Nervousness, Loss of Appetite, ratulence. Low Spirits, Sleeplessness, and Chest Affec- tions. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is entirely vegetable, and contains neither iron nor mercury, nor any injurious mineral substances, which accumulate in the system when taken in medicine. and cause future pain and trouble. Gwilym Evans' QUitlitlB Bitters is a Natural 132medy, containing a most nappy combination of Quinine with the active principles of the best known an-1 most valuable plants, which have not hitherto been saccessfully dispensed. Now Indigestion assumes so many forms that there is scsrcely a complaint which it may not resemble in one way or another. It has not been inaptly termed " Oir National Disease." There is no disease more prevalent or more difficult to cure. It is a disease of the stomach, and assumes a variety of different forms in parts of the body far removed from the stomach. The only trustworthy and permanent remedy is Gwilym Evans' Qdinine Bitters, which, acting upon the digestive organs, strengthens them and stimu- lates them to healthy action, and gives tone to toe whole stomach, imparting new life, hope, strength, had happiness. NERVOUS DISORDERS.</p>
        <p>Nervous disorders are generally traceable to defectivc. digestion. Most nervous people are dyspeptic also. The stomach does not digest the food ; the necessary supply of vital particles which the blood should receive from properly digested food fails, and the result is felt almost immediately upon the most sensitive portions of the human organism—the nerves. Impure blood irritates the nerves and causes nervous weakness. This renders the nervous system very liable to be affected by unhealthy influences. In nine cases out:of ten, if the imperfect digestion be remedied, the nervousness and weakness will disappear. The only certain remedy is Gwilym Evans' Qiinine Bitters, sold everywhere in bottles 23. 91 and 4s. 63. each, or will be sent, carriage free, on receipt of stamps, direct, by the Sole Propriet. ors : —T13,3 Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited, Llanelly, South Wales. Beware of Imita- tions. The name " Gwilyea Evacs" must be found en the label, on the scamp, and on the bottle, to ensure its being genuine. Be sure you get the right article when you ask for it. Do not be put off with substitutes. No their preparation is " Just as good "or " Toe same biog."</p>
