        <p>played. Won. D'n. Lost. Cr ag't Pt, Bewsey All Saints 9 ... 7 ... 2 ... 0 ... 34... 8... 16 Wllderspool Central 8 ... 7 ... 1 ... 0 ... 27... 4... 15 Widnes St. Mary's Weston Church Mariners' Church Halton View Juniors 9 ... 6 ... 0 ... 3 ... 21... 11... 12 Appleton White Star 9 ... 4 ... 2 ... 3 ... 21... 13... 10 Widnes Albert.... ...... 10 ... 4 .. 2 ... 4 ... 13... 18... 10 Weston Church Re've 7 ... 4... 1... 2 ... 15... 11... 9 Penketh 5 . 4 0 1 . 13.... 3... 8 Howley Frod.ham Parish Ch 7 ... 4 ... 0 ... 3 ... 20... 10... 8 Richmond's West Bank Juniors RUNC3RN PARISH CHURCH v. SANKEY Atntoxe. Played a fliendlr on the giound of the former on Saturday, in a dense fog, which almost made the players invisible to the spectators. A good hard game WAI given. Parish proving slightly the superior. From a fine exhibition of combination by ad the forwards Johnson shot to centre and Price headed the ball into the not This privet the only score, the home team winning by one goal to nil.</p>
        <p>LATCHFORD VICIORIL xr LATCHFORD JUNIORS.</p>
        <p>Playe-d-On-Saturday on the ground of th 3 former. The play soon went to the Vies', goal, but Unsworth the goal- keeper. sr.ved in smart style. After some give-and-take play Hazelhurst score i for tho visitors. Half-time arrived with the Juniors leading by one goal to nil. After the re- start play hardly ever reached the home gnat, and Shake shaft snored a well-earned goal. Both sides tried hard to get the lead, but time came with the selre one goal each. RIT!ICORK PARISH RECS V PSNKETEI FRIE/D4' SCHOOL.</p>
        <p>- -- This encounter to)k place at Penkoth on Saturday. A thick fog enveloped the ground. but play was quite possible. Runcorn started and immediately att +eked. but were driven back. Shortly afterwards,while play was in the home team's goal mouth, Tudor rushed in and scored for the visitors. Parish continued to hold the advantage till half-time, when they were leading by to goals to nil, both goals being from the foot of 3 Tudor. On resuminr, Penketh pressed vigor* lously, and Barton scored with a hard shot. Shortly atter- terwards, Hulse, the visitors' goal, was again called upon to deleted, but he was equal to th • occasion. Later, Silvia and Robinson both scored tor the visitors, who led at the final by four goals to one.</p>
