        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON LANCASHIRE COUNTY (LUNATIC ASYLUMS). At a Special Meeting of the Council of the Borough of Warrington held on the 9th day of November, 1901 at the Town Hall pursuant to the Borough Funds Act,1372, the following resolution was passed by an absolute majority of the Council That tiro Council do jointly with other Lancashire County Boroughs promote during the ensuing Session of Parliament. " A Bill to alter and amend the Lancashire County (Lunatic Asylums and other powers) Act, 1391, and to alter the mode of contribution to the expenses of the Lancashire Asylums Board " and that the costs and expenses attending the same shall be chargeable upon and payable out of the Borough Ford and that the Council are hereby authorised under and in pursuance of " An Act to authorise the application of funds of Municipal Corporations and other governing bodies in certain cases "to apply such Borough Fund to the pay- ment of such costs and expenses accordingly. DATED this 15th day of November 1901. J. LYON WHITTLE, Town Clerk. Town Hall, Warrington.</p>
